# What `railway up` must NOT upload.
#
# `.dockerignore` governs the BUILD CONTEXT; this governs the UPLOAD, and they
# are different steps. Without this, `railway up` tars node_modules and the
# upload can time out before a build ever starts — which produces a deployment
# row stuck at INITIALIZING with no build logs, reading exactly like a broken
# build when it is not.
#
# NOTE: no `!` negation anywhere. Railway's ignore parser does not honour it, so
# a negated rule silently excludes what it claims to keep.
node_modules
e2e
